{"type": "message", "id": "234d084f", "parentId": "4a762815", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T06:01:35.045Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "tool-4395f45e756e48bcaa1a45d708febe8f", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"site:wikipedia.org \\\"NAEP\\\" 2022 grade 8 mathematics state scores\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 3,\n  \"tookMs\": 852,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2ee00e4858de5d5d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNational Assessment of Educational Progress - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2ee00e4858de5d5d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Assessment_of_Educational_Progress\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f0d1e7bde5ff42b8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNCES will &quot;project&quot;, state and district-level scores on TIMSS in both subjects using data from NAEP. The NIES is a two-part study designed to describe the condition of education for American Indian/Alaska Native students in the United States. The first part of the study consists of assessment results in mathematics and reading at grades 4 and 8.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f0d1e7bde5ff42b8\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 15, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1d55a3fb861ef647\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNational Center for Education Statistics - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1d55a3fb861ef647\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Center_for_Education_Statistics\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6a5753ce9cfe9977\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP), a nationwide assessment of achievement among primary and secondary students\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6a5753ce9cfe9977\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 22, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9b8675712d86eeee\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMathematics education in the United States - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9b8675712d86eeee\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematics_education_in_the_United_States\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"10ab3b2ca57f0000\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn mathematics, only <strong>26% were proficient</strong>, even though 90% of the parents asked thought their children met grade standards. Having a higher NAEP math score in eighth grade is correlated with high academic standing, higher income, lower rates of adolescent parenthood, and lower chances of criminality.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"10ab3b2ca57f0000\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"18 hours ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.m.wikipedia.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:wikipedia.org \"NAEP\" 2022 grade 8 mathematics state scores", "provider": "brave", "count": 3, "tookMs": 852, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2ee00e4858de5d5d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNational Assessment of Educational Progress - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2ee00e4858de5d5d\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Assessment_of_Educational_Progress", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f0d1e7bde5ff42b8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNCES will &quot;project&quot;, state and district-level scores on TIMSS in both subjects using data from NAEP. The NIES is a two-part study designed to describe the condition of education for American Indian/Alaska Native students in the United States. The first part of the study consists of assessment results in mathematics and reading at grades 4 and 8.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f0d1e7bde5ff42b8\">>>", "published": "February 15, 2026", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1d55a3fb861ef647\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNational Center for Education Statistics - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1d55a3fb861ef647\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Center_for_Education_Statistics", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6a5753ce9cfe9977\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP), a nationwide assessment of achievement among primary and secondary students\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6a5753ce9cfe9977\">>>", "published": "July 22, 2025", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9b8675712d86eeee\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMathematics education in the United States - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9b8675712d86eeee\">>>", "url": "https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematics_education_in_the_United_States", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"10ab3b2ca57f0000\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn mathematics, only <strong>26% were proficient</strong>, even though 90% of the parents asked thought their children met grade standards. Having a higher NAEP math score in eighth grade is correlated with high academic standing, higher income, lower rates of adolescent parenthood, and lower chances of criminality.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"10ab3b2ca57f0000\">>>", "published": "18 hours ago", "siteName": "en.m.wikipedia.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775282495044}}
